{"t": 1794123755.6804, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Production regression introduced by this change (suspect commit 8c2f1d0): Sentry LEDGER-WORKER-9A reports ReconciliationMismatch, expected 1100 minor units but got 1099, first seen in ledger-worker@2026.11.3.\n\nError: https://sentry.io/organizations/acme/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/\n\nThe replacement of Decimal rounding with int(amount_minor * rate) truncates instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit. The local fix in worker/rates.py uses round(amount_minor * rate). A synthetic regression check with amount_minor=1000 and rate=1.0999999999999999 reproduces 1099 with the old implementation and returns 1100 with the fix. Six direct checks passed, including positive/negative amounts and zero; the local pytest invocation discovered no tests. The exact prior Decimal tie-breaking policy could not be retrieved, so half-unit compatibility is not verified.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
